WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:17.141
About one week after Heidi started praying, the tutor asked to speak with Clara's grandmother.

2
00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:20.873
He wanted to tell her about something remarkable.

3
00:00:20.874 --> 00:00:25.647
"Something I had stopped hoping for has happened," said the tutor.

4
00:00:25.648 --> 00:00:29.781
"It can only be looked upon as a miracle."

5
00:00:29.782 --> 00:00:34.565
"Has Heidi learned to read at last?" asked Grandmamma.

6
00:00:34.566 --> 00:00:37.781
The tutor looked at the lady with astonishment.

7
00:00:37.782 --> 00:00:42.679
"How did you guess?" he asked. "It is truly marvelous!

8
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.039
At first she seemed unable to learn her letters.

9
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.267
Now it is as if she has learned them overnight."

10
00:00:50.268 --> 00:00:53.835
"Many unlikely things happen in life,"

11
00:00:53.836 --> 00:00:56.957
said Grandmamma with a pleased smile.

12
00:00:56.958 --> 00:01:01.939
Grandmamma was so pleased that she wanted to reward Heidi with a present.

13
00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.445
She found her reading aloud to Clara.

14
00:01:04.446 --> 00:01:09.675
"Heidi, I am so pleased that you have learned to read.

15
00:01:09.676 --> 00:01:14.950
The picture book is yours to keep," Grandmamma said.

16
00:01:14.951 --> 00:01:17.973
Heidi was overwhelmed with delight.

17
00:01:17.974 --> 00:01:20.604
"Mine to keep always?

18
00:01:20.605 --> 00:01:25.034
Even when I go home?" said Heidi, blushing with pleasure.

19
00:01:25.035 --> 00:01:31.906
"Yes, of course, yours forever," Grandmamma assured her.

20
00:01:31.907 --> 00:01:37.394
When Heidi went to bed that night, she looked at her book again before falling asleep.

21
00:01:37.395 --> 00:01:43.148
From that day forward, her chief pleasure was to read over and over again

22
00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:49.382
the tales that belonged to the beautiful pictures of the shepherd and his flock.

23
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:54.865
Heidi often went to Grandmamma's room in the afternoons while Clara took her nap.

24
00:01:54.866 --> 00:01:59.338
There she learned to sew, and Grandmamma listened to Heidi read aloud.

25
00:01:59.339 --> 00:02:03.006
All the people Heidi read about became like dear friends.

26
00:02:03.007 --> 00:02:05.751
It always delighted her to be with them.

27
00:02:05.752 --> 00:02:09.572
But Heidi's homesickness never left her.

28
00:02:09.573 --> 00:02:15.561
In the last week of her visit, Grandmamma called Heidi into her room one evening after dinner.

29
00:02:15.562 --> 00:02:21.360
"Now, child," she said, "tell me why you are not happy?

30
00:02:21.361 --> 00:02:26.038
Do you still have the same trouble in your heart?"

31
00:02:26.039 --> 00:02:28.440
Heidi nodded in reply.

32
00:02:28.441 --> 00:02:31.217
"Have you told God about it?"

33
00:02:31.218 --> 00:02:34.338
"Yes," said Heidi, sadly.

34
00:02:34.339 --> 00:02:42.400
"And do you pray every night to ask God to make things right so that you may be happy again?"

35
00:02:42.401 --> 00:02:46.460
"No, I have stopped praying," said Heidi.

36
00:02:46.461 --> 00:02:49.817
Grandmamma was surprised.

37
00:02:49.818 --> 00:02:52.193
"Do not tell me that!

38
00:02:52.194 --> 00:02:56.053
Why have you stopped praying?"

39
00:02:56.054 --> 00:02:58.403
"It doesn't do any good.

40
00:02:58.404 --> 00:03:03.291
God does not listen," Heidi said in an agitated voice.

41
00:03:03.292 --> 00:03:08.536
"How can He listen when so many people pray to Him every night?

42
00:03:08.537 --> 00:03:10.808
He cannot hear them all.

43
00:03:10.809 --> 00:03:15.099
He certainly has not heard what I said to Him."

44
00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.689
"You are wrong, Heidi.

45
00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.585
You must not think of Him like that.

46
00:03:20.586 --> 00:03:22.697
God has heard you.

47
00:03:22.698 --> 00:03:29.964
If He has not given you what you prayed for, He will give you something better when the time is right.

48
00:03:29.965 --> 00:03:33.494
He knows better than we do what is good for us.

49
00:03:33.495 --> 00:03:37.737
Continue to pray and to trust Him."

50
00:03:37.738 --> 00:03:44.158
Heidi had perfect confidence in Grandmamma, and every word she said sank into her heart.

51
00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:50.727
That night, Heidi prayed once again so that God would go on thinking about her.

52
00:03:50.728 --> 00:03:53.617
The day came for Grandmamma to leave.

53
00:03:53.618 --> 00:04:05.414
Both Clara and Heidi were very sad, but all morning, Grandmamma kept them lively and amused with songs and games so that they had no time to be unhappy.

54
00:04:05.415 --> 00:04:09.471
After she had left, the house seemed silent and empty.

55
00:04:09.472 --> 00:04:16.604
Clara and Heidi sat the remainder of the day like two lost children.
